 .PP
 With the
+.B -t
+flag, cooked input is echoed for an ANSI text terminal with the given
+width (at least 8 columns).  Erasing characters clears their cells,
+including tabs, wide characters and wrapped lines; ctl-U erases only
+editable input, leaving the prompt intact.  The caller supplies the
+terminal width when starting the session.
+Without this flag, console echo retains the usual backspace semantics.
+.PP
